Include relations.

Let R be relation.

Lemma: R is symmetric implies R = (R⁻¹).
Proof:
    Assume R is symmetric.
    Proof R ⊆ (R⁻¹):
        Assume R[x,y].
        Then R[y,x] by symmetry.
        Hence (R⁻¹)[x,y].
    qed.
    Proof (R⁻¹) ⊆ R:
        Assume (R⁻¹)[x,y].
        Then R[y,x].
        Then R[x,y] by symmetry.
    qed.
    Hence R = (R⁻¹).
qed.
